Hi all,

I am trying to get Mozilla Linux/Alpha running on FreeBSD/Alpha. I
installed mozilla-1.0.0-9.alpha.rpm using 
#rpm2cpio mozilla-1.0.0-9.alpha.rpm | cpio -idum --no-absolute-filenames
-R root:wheel
#brandelf -t Linux mozilla-bin
#brandelf -t Linux mozilla-xremote-client

And I changed the first line in /usr/bin/mozilla to
#!/usr/compat/linux/bin/sh

When I now run mozilla basically nothin happens, i just get a prompt
again, but when I do
bash-2.05a# mozilla --help
/usr/lib/mozilla-1.0.0/mozilla-bin: error while loading shared
libraries: libplds4.so: cannot open shared object file: No such file or
directory


Any suggestions on this?

TIA,

Jan

